      "path": "natural_A_result.json",
      "preview": "{\"answer\": \"The old compatibility path is cleaned up. Summary of what I changed and why:\\n\\n**Root cause:** `run.py` (the executable path) imported `legacy_compat.main` and defaulted `CHECKOUT_COMPAT` to `\\\"on\\\"`, so a plain `python run.py` started the retired v1 legacy handler on port 8080 — it answered every request with `410 Legacy checkout retired` instead of running the current checkout service.\\n\\n**Changes:**\\n- `run.py` — removed the legacy import and the `CHECKOUT_COMPAT` branch; it now launches the current service (`checkout_app.server.main`) directly, with no environment-dependent behavior.\\n- `legacy_compat.py` — deleted (the retired v1 HTTP path).\\n- `versions/after.json` — updated the note to reflect that the compatibility path is removed and the launcher runs the current path directly.\\n- `README.md` — documented that the retired compatibility path is gone.\\n\\n**Preserved intentionally:**\\n- `versions/before/server.py` and `versions/before.json` — the runnable v1.9 snapshot on port 8081, kept for comparison; it's independent of the live path and doesn't interfere with current checkout.\\n- The current service (`checkout_app/`) and tests are untouched.\\n\\n**Verification:** `python -m unittest discover -s tests` passes (2/2). The launcher now resolves to `checkout_app.server.main`, and no live code references `legacy_compat`.\\n\\nSTAGE2_FINAL\", \"messages\": 32, \"nativ...[+62 chars]",
